    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nSetting \"globs\" is already supported by `Pick grep`, but only statically. It would be great if it could also support setting the globs interactively via `<C-o>` just like `grep_live` does.\n\nUse case:\nSince I often have to deal with large repos or have to browse ignored folders for auto-generated files being able to sometimes glob to limit the search directories and thus also the amount of hits is very handy.\n\nThank you very much!\n\n",
