        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI think it is more reasonable design-wise to keep `grep` picker more \"pre-define everything, search via CLI tool, and use built-in matching\". While `grep_live` is more \"use CLI tool to search by interactively adjusting its parameters\".\n\nMy suggestion would be to use `grep_live` picker and set its pattern. One common usage can be to use something like `<C-r><C-w>` to insert a word under cursor (this [by default works for any picker](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-pick.html#minipick-actions-paste)).\n\nClosing as not planned. If you have a more involved workflow with `grep` specifically, we can figure out a better way to do it with `grep_live`.",
