        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Supports special cases of register: <C-f> (as [c_CTRL-R_CTRL-F](https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag.html?tag=c_CTRL-R_CTRL-F)), <C-w> (as [c_CTRL-R_CTRL-W](https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag.html?tag=c_CTRL-R_CTRL-W)), <C-a> (as [c_CTRL-R_CTRL-A](https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag.html?tag=c_CTRL-R_CTRL-A)), <C-l> (as [c_CTRL-R_CTRL-L](https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag.html?tag=c_CTRL-R_CTRL-L)).\n\nHow did I miss this in the doc .... this solves like 99% of my problems. Thank you!\n\nofftopic:\nThe other thing I was missing was a toggle/option to also searching in ignored paths, but I solved that with a custom `rg -uu` picker like you suggested in one of the discussion about this topic. For grep_live glob-ing for \"*\" works, so I only needed one for files.",
